# Insulet MuleSoft Design Standards Reference

> **Purpose:** Internal context for the design agent. Apply these standards when generating
> design documents to ensure the output is consistent with what the develop, RAML, and review
> agents will enforce. Full canonical rules are in `agents/review/rules/` and
> `agents/raml/rules/`. This file is a compact design-phase digest.

---

## 1. API & Project Naming

**Rule:** `{name}-{layer}-api` — no regional prefix, lower-case, hyphen-separated.
- ✅ `payments-sys-api`, `drupal-exp-api`, `benefits-investigation-proc-api`
- ❌ `na-payments-sys-api`, `NA_Payments_SYS_API`

**Layers:** `sys` (system), `proc` (process), `exp` (experience)

**Max length:** 42 characters (Anypoint Runtime Manager limit). Use short forms if needed: `##-##-sapi`, `##-##-papi`, `##-##-xapi`.

**RAML spec name:** `{name}-{layer}-api-spec` (e.g., `payments-sys-api-spec`)
**Root RAML file name** must match the project name: `payments-sys-api-spec.raml`

**Exchange asset title:** User-friendly Title Case (e.g., `sfl-leads-sys-api-spec` → `SFL Leads System API`)

**Canonical rule:** `agents/review/rules/review-api-design-standards.mdc`

---

## 2. URL Pattern

```
Base path:  /{api-technical-name}/api/{version}/
Health:     GET /api/ping
            GET /api/health-check
Business:   plural noun collections (e.g., /customers/profiles, /orders, /payments)
```

- Collections use **plural** nouns (e.g., `/customers/profiles`)
- Singular resources use **singular** nouns (e.g., `/customer/{id}`)
- Version in URL = major semver only: `v1`, `v2`
- **baseUri is MANDATORY** in every root RAML: `baseUri: https://api.example.com/{project-name}/api/{version}`
- **Canonical rule:** `agents/review/rules/review-api-design-standards.mdc`

---

## 3. Flow & Sub-Flow Naming

When documenting planned flow names in the design, use these patterns:

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Main API flow | `{api-spec-name}-main` | `payments-sys-api-spec-main` |
| APIKit flows | `{method}:\{resource}:{api-config}` | Do NOT rename — APIKit-generated |
| Business flows | `{descriptive-name}-flow` | `create-customer-profile-flow` |
| Sub-flows | `{descriptive-name}-sub-flow` | `resolve-authnet-credentials-sub-flow` |
| Flow XML files | lower-case-hyphenated `.xml` | `create-customer-profile.xml` |

**Message Processor `doc:name`:** Never leave default Anypoint Studio names on processors (e.g., "Transform Message", "Set Variable"). Use descriptive, readable names in Title Case.
- Transforms: `FV` prefix for variable-setting (optional, minor), `DW` prefix for payload (optional, minor)
- HTTP Requests: describe the target system (e.g., `REQUEST USPS SYS API`)
- Custom Logger: describe the log point (e.g., `Log Entry`, `Log Exit`, `Log Error`)

**Canonical rule:** `agents/review/rules/review-mule-flow-naming.mdc`

