## 5. Logging Standards

**Always use `module-logger` (Insulet Custom Logger Connector). Never use built-in Mule `logger`.**

| Operation | Default Level | When to Use |
|---|---|---|
| `build-log-without-payload` | INFO | Flow milestones, metadata — no payload |
| `build-log-with-masked-payload` | DEBUG | Debugging structure with sensitive fields as `***` |
| `build-log-with-encrypted-payload` | DEBUG | Full AES-256-CBC encrypted payload for compliance/audit |
| `build-error-log-without-payload` | INFO/ERROR | Error context without payload |
| `build-error-log-with-masked-payload` | DEBUG | Error with masked payload for triage |
| `build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload` | DEBUG | Error with encrypted payload for incident recovery |

**Log categories (packages):**

| Category | Level | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `com.insulet.general` | INFO | Milestones and metadata. No payload allowed. |
| `com.insulet.maskedpayload` | DEBUG | Masked payloads for debugging structure |
| `com.insulet.encryptedpayload` | DEBUG | Fully encrypted payloads for compliance/audits |

**Connector defaults:** The connector auto-sets `category` based on the operation when not explicitly provided. Absent `category` is acceptable (minor); mismatched `category` is a Major violation.

**Required attributes on every logger:** `config-ref`, `message`, `sourceSystem`, `targetSystem`, `tracepoint`, `category`

**Standardized tracepoints (use only these values):**
- `FLOW_START` / `FLOW_END`
- `BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST` / `AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST`
- `BEFORE_DB_CALL` / `AFTER_DB_CALL`
- `BEFORE_SALESFORCE` / `AFTER_SALESFORCE`
- `CRITICAL_CHECKPOINT`
- `VALIDATION`
- `APPLICATION_EVENT`
- `TRANSFORMATION`
- `EXCEPTION`

**Connector default for `tracepoint`:** `FLOW_START`. Must be set explicitly when context requires a different value:
- Error handlers → must explicitly set `EXCEPTION` (Major if absent or wrong)
- Exit loggers → must explicitly set `FLOW_END` (Major if absent)
- Entry loggers → `FLOW_START` default is correct (Minor best practice to make explicit)

**Log4j2 configuration:** Single `log4j2.xml` file — no env-specific log4j files. Declare three `AsyncLogger` entries:
```xml
<AsyncLogger name="com.insulet.general" level="INFO" />
<AsyncLogger name="com.insulet.maskedpayload" level="DEBUG" />
<AsyncLogger name="com.insulet.encryptedpayload" level="DEBUG" />
```

**PROD policy:** `DEBUG` is only allowed temporarily during active triage — must be reverted. For PROD, set `com.insulet.*` categories to `WARN` via Maven resource filtering or deployment configuration.

**Global connector configuration must include:**
- `sensitiveKeyParts` — comma-separated PII/credential field fragments (e.g., `ssn,password,secret,token,email,cardNumber`)
- `safeKeys` — keys to exclude from masking (e.g., `passwordPolicy`)
- `encryptionKey` — Base64-encoded 256-bit AES key, sourced from secure vault only
- `entityDetails` — must contain **only** non-sensitive business identifiers (e.g., `orderId`)

**Cross-cutting concerns — do NOT show in architecture diagrams:**
- Request-context capture (log entry/exit)
- Correlation-ID propagation
- API Manager policy enforcement

Document these once in a prefatory paragraph at the top of the Backend Mapping & Logic section.

**Canonical rule:** `agents/review/rules/review-logging-standards.mdc`

